    "relation": "derives-from"
  },
  {
    "action": {
      "autoEmit": true,
      "capabilityProfile": "research-worker",
      "maxIterations": 4,
      "model": "deepseek-v4-flash:cloud",
      "modelId": "research-scout",
      "nl": "You classify ONE article for a research brief. You do NOT count, date, or route anything — those are already computed and must be copied through verbatim.\n\nDOMAIN: ${config.data.topic}\n${config.data.domainHint}\n\nARTICLE\nurl: ${input.data.url}\ntitle: ${input.data.title}\nextract: ${input.data.extract}\n\nAssign EXACTLY ONE category, using one of these strings verbatim:\n${config.data.categories}\n\nIf none fits, use \"unrelated\". Prefer an existing category over inventing a near-duplicate.\n\nYour FINAL answer must be exactly one JSON object, no markdown fences:\n{\"url\":\"${input.data.url}\",\"recency\":\"${input.data.recency}\",\"publishedAt\":\"${input.data.publishedAt}\",\"title\":\"${input.data.title}\",\"blobUrn\":\"${input.data.blobUrn}\",\"briefId\":\"${input.data.briefId}\",\"category\":\"...\",\"summary\":\"one or two sentences on the angle it takes\",\"keyPoints\":[\"...\",\"...\"],\"confidence\":\"high|medium|low\"}\n\nCopy url, recency, publishedAt, title, blobUrn and briefId EXACTLY as given. Do not recompute or omit them. blobUrn is the ONLY pointer to the stored full text: this lane's answer object REPLACES the token, so a field you leave out is lost for good.",
      "role": "rw-h-",
      "timeoutMs": 240000,
      "type": "agent"
    },
    "id": "t-scout-categorize",
    "kind": "agent",
    "label": "Categorise one article (domain from brief)",
    "metadata": {
      "netId": "scout",
      "sessionId": "dev-support-council"
    },
    "mode": "SINGLE",
    "postsets": {
      "out": {
        "host": "research-scout@agentic-net-node:8080",
        "placeId": "p-scout-analysis"
      }
    },
    "presets": {
      "config": {
        "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.active == \"true\" LIMIT 1",
        "consume": false,
        "host": "research-scout@agentic-net-node:8080",
        "optional": false,
        "placeId": "p-scout-brief",
        "take": "FIRST"
      },
      "input": {
        "arcql": "FROM $ LIMIT 1",
        "consume": true,
        "host": "research-scout@agentic-net-node:8080",
        "placeId": "p-scout-candidates",
        "take": "FIRST"
      }
    },
    "role": "rw-h-"
  },
  {
    "action": {
      "autoEmit": true,
      "capabilityProfile": "research-worker",
      "maxIterations": 8,
      "model": "deepseek-v4-pro:cloud",
      "modelId": "research-scout",
      "nl": "You are an analyst working this brief:\n\nTOPIC: ${config.data.topic}\n${config.data.description}\n\nYou get two kinds of input and must treat them differently.\n\nFACTS — computed deterministically from the crawl. Every number is measured. Do NOT recount,\nre-derive, or estimate any figure; quote them exactly. If a number you want is not there, say\nso rather than inventing it.\n${input.data.factsJson}\n\nFRESH ARTICLES — the actual body text of every recently published competitor article\n(${input.data.freshTextArticles} of them). This is evidence, not counts. Some are clipped;\n`truncated` says which. Read them to say what the competition is ACTUALLY arguing right now,\nnot merely how many pieces they shipped.\n${input.data.freshTextJson}\n\nWrite the analysis. Cover:\n1. Which angles the sources clearly OWN — categories with the most coverage, and who leads each.\n2. FRESHNESS — who publishes recently versus sits on ageing content, using the brand-new/recent/archive split.\n3. FRESH SIGNAL — from the article text only: the specific problems, sub-topics and framings the\n   recent pieces cover, the depth they go to, and what they conspicuously leave out. Quote or\n   closely paraphrase concrete details so a reader can tell you actually read them. If two fresh\n   pieces converge on one theme, name that theme — a competitor segmenting a topic is the single\n   strongest signal of where they see demand.\n4. GAPS — categories and angles thinly covered or absent, i.e. the openings worth taking.\n5. Three concrete recommendations. Each must name the gap it exploits, the source it targets, and\n   where possible the fresh-article weakness it beats. Ground them in the text, not just the counts.\n\nBe specific. Name sources by host. No preamble, no restating the brief.\n\nEverything you need is already in this prompt — there is nothing to look up, so do NOT call\nTHINK, and do not query anything. Deliver the result by calling DONE exactly once, on your\nFIRST iteration, passing the JSON object below as its `summary` argument. DONE is the only\nchannel that returns an answer here: prose written outside a DONE call is discarded, and an\niteration budget spent thinking produces nothing at all.\n\nYour FINAL answer must be exactly one JSON object, no markdown fences:\n{\"kind\":\"landscape-analysis\",\"generatedAt\":\"${input.data.generatedAt}\",\"totalFindings\":\"${input.data.totalFindings}\",\"freshTextArticles\":\"${input.data.freshTextArticles}\",\"ownedAngles\":\"...\",\"freshness\":\"...\",\"freshSignal\":\"...\",\"gaps\":\"...\",\"recommendations\":[\"...\",\"...\",\"...\"]}",
      "role": "rw-h-",
      "timeoutMs": 300000,
      "type": "agent"
    },
    "id": "t-scout-digest",
    "kind": "agent",
    "label": "Landscape analysis (facts + fresh full text)",
    "metadata": {
      "netId": "scout",
      "sessionId": "dev-support-council"
    },
    "mode": "SINGLE",
    "postsets": {
      "out": {
        "host": "research-scout@agentic-net-node:8080",
        "placeId": "p-scout-digest",
        "retain": 3
      }
    },
    "presets": {
      "config": {
        "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.active == \"true\" LIMIT 1",
        "consume": false,
        "host": "research-scout@agentic-net-node:8080",
        "optional": false,
        "placeId": "p-scout-brief",
        "take": "FIRST"
      },
      "input": {
        "arcql": "FROM $ WHERE $.kind == \"facts\" LIMIT 1",
        "consume": true,
        "host": "research-scout@agentic-net-node:8080",
        "placeId": "p-scout-taxonomy",
        "take": "FIRST"
      }
    },
    "role": "rw-h-"
  },
  {
    "action": {
      "await": "ALL",
      "dispatch": [
        {
          "channel": "default",
          "executor": "bash"
        }
      ],
      "executorId": "agentic-net-executor-default",
      "groupBy": "executor",
      "inputPlace": "input",
      "timeoutMs": 180000,
      "type": "command"
    },
    "emit": [
      {
        "from": "@result",
        "to": "log"
      }
    ],
